# Normalise to LF in the repository, and check out LF everywhere.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf on a Windows clone restores CRLF into the working tree, and the very
# next `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` fails on line endings alone - on a machine where nothing
# was actually edited. The CI job runs on Linux and would still pass, so the break would only ever
# be visible locally, which is the worst place for it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git never tries to normalise or diff them as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.snk  binary
*.pfx  binary
